[h1]Timeline Extended + Better Politics — Compatibility [Experimental][/h1]

Independent compatibility patch for Victoria 3 1.15.0. Requires both parent mods.
This is an experimental 0.6.0-dev candidate, not a completed compatibility release.

[h2]Load order — top to bottom[/h2]
[list]
[*]Timeline Extended
[*]Better Politics Mod — full version, not Lite
[*]This compatibility patch — last
[/list]
Disable duplicate local/Workshop copies. Start a new single-player campaign.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*]Integrates 70 shared laws and political stances for 39 additional TE law groups.
[*]Adapts parties, elections, characters, production, institutions and overlapping UI.
[*]Connects TE tax proposals and reforms to all 21 BPM interest groups.
[*]Resolves conflicting event/value definitions and duplicate law-checkpoint effects.
[*]Bounds cabinet candidate selection and clears temporary candidate lists.
[*]Reduces repeated cabinet consensus scans while preserving the original formula.
[/list]

[h2]Validation and limitations[/h2]
61 synthetic tests passed: 400 consensus comparisons and 5000 candidate turnover
cycles, plus reference and call-graph checks. These are offline tests, not an
engine benchmark. Loading, UI, save/reload, late-era balance and real performance
still require gameplay testing. Old-save and multiplayer compatibility are unverified.

The checked source baseline is TE 1.3.0 commit 48a28e73 and full BPM 2.5 commit
d785d399, with Victoria 3 1.15.0. Workshop TE differed in 12 checked files from
that baseline. Future Workshop updates are not automatically covered.

